## 10. Deployment & CI/CD

### 10.1. Build Pipeline

```bash
npm run build
```

Vite outputs optimized assets to `dist/`.

### 10.2. Hosting Options

| Platform | Features | Pricing |
|----------|----------|---------|
| Vercel | Edge functions, CDN, preview URLs | Free tier, $20/mo for pro |
| Netlify | Functions, form handling, split testing | Free tier, $19/mo for pro |
| Cloudflare Pages | Zero‑config, CDN, Workers | Free tier, $20/mo for pro |
| AWS Amplify | Managed hosting, CI/CD, auth | Free tier, pay-as-you-go |

### 10.3. CI/CD Example (GitHub Actions)

```yaml
name: CI

on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:

jobs:
  build-test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: '20'
          cache: 'npm'
      - run: npm ci
      - run: npm run lint
      - run: npm run test -- --coverage
      - run: npm run build
      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
        with:
          name: dist
          path: dist/
```

Deploy to Vercel automatically on push to `main`:

```yaml
deploy:
  needs: build-test
  runs-on: ubuntu-latest
  steps:
    - uses: actions/download-artifact@v4
      with:
        name: dist
        path: dist
    - uses: amondnet/vercel-action@v20
      with:
        vercel-token: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_TOKEN }}
        vercel-org-id: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_ORG_ID }}
        vercel-project-id: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_PROJECT_ID }}
        vercel-args: '--prod'
```

